PUBLIC RESPONSE: {E. tell

The refrain-loop account from Colleagues 1–3 and 5 continues to hold the strongest match to the actual audio track that is audible under the filmed twist sequence. The right → left → right weight shift is visibly locked to the three successive statements of the title hook that open the Jack Rabbit Slim’s number, placing the second right-leg accent on the stressed syllable “tell.”  

That said, I share some of the verse-timing concern raised by Colleagues 4, 6 and 7: the camera pull-back does occur slightly earlier than the third full refrain iteration, which could make the visible accent read as landing on the second rather than the third repetition of the hook. If that micro-timing discrepancy holds up under closer review, it would still keep the accent on the same word “tell” within the looped vocal rather than shifting it back to any verse syllable. The non-existent “Pierre did truly love the mademoiselle” line remains the decisive flaw in the B-camp reconstruction; once that is set aside, the remaining audible lyric material points to the refrain hook even if the exact count of repetitions needs one more frame check.}

