PUBLIC RESPONSE: {E. tell

The three-beat right-left-right cycle still lines up most cleanly with the audible refrain loop that opens the Jack Rabbit Slim’s sequence. Colleagues 4 and 7’s verse-entry timing is worth another look, but the camera pull-back and heel-snap occur just after the second full “You never can tell,” which would place the return accent on the third iteration of the same stressed syllable. That keeps the second right-leg exaggeration on “tell” rather than any earlier verse word.

The only remaining uncertainty is whether the visible switch is counted as the second or third repetition of the hook; a single extra frame or two could shift the exact count, but it would still land on the same refrain syllable rather than moving the accent back into the verse. Once the non-existent “Pierre” line is set aside, the audible vocal track continues to favor the looped title word.}

